    <!-- SECTION FOUR: ARCHITECTURE & DATA FLOW -->
    <h2 id="runtime-architecture">4. Architecture & Data Flow</h2>
    <p>The demo suite relies on a decoupled, non-destructive architecture that keeps rendering and physics perfectly synchronized:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Zero-Cost Mesh Geometry:</strong> Terrain meshes do not require <code>Read/Write Enabled</code> in their import settings[cite: 4]. Base vertex colors and weights remain strictly on the GPU, protecting memory budgets on consoles and mobile devices[cite: 4].</li>
        <li><strong>Tri-Biome Runtime Ledger:</strong> When terrain is baked via <code>DPT_SurfaceDataBaker</code>, the system packs the three candidate biomes (<code>id0, id1, id2</code>) and their base unscaled weights (<code>w0, w1</code>) into contiguous byte arrays inside <code>DPT_TerrainSurfaceData</code>[cite: 9]. This requires only 5 bytes per triangle (~150 KB for a 30,000-triangle mesh).</li>
        <li><strong>On-Demand Evaluation:</strong> When <code>DPT_SurfaceRaycastTester</code> hits a triangle, <code>DPT_TerrainSurfaceTarget</code> queries the material's current vector properties (<code>_Dynamic_Biome_Slot1</code>, etc.). It multiplies only the matching candidate weights for that single hit triangle and immediately returns the winner.</li>
        <li><strong>Exact Visual/Audio Parity:</strong> If snow accumulates from a dusting to full coverage via <code>DPT_DynamicBiomeDemoController</code>, the raycast query dynamically transitions from returning Grass to returning Mountain Snow at the exact threshold where snow takes over visually[cite: 6].</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- SECTION FIVE: TROUBLESHOOTING -->
    <h2 id="troubleshooting">5. Troubleshooting Notes</h2>
    
    <div class="troubleshooting-q">"The Raycast Tester reports 'None' or does not detect any surface."</div>
    <div class="troubleshooting-a">Ensure the terrain GameObject has an active <code>MeshCollider</code> attached and that its physics layer is included in the <code>Raycast Layers</code> mask. Also verify that <code>DPT_TerrainSurfaceTarget</code> is present on the same GameObject and references a valid baked <code>DPT_TerrainSurfaceData</code> asset[cite: 9].</div>

    <div class="troubleshooting-q">"Live Biome Modifiers are changing the visuals, but raycasts still return the old baked biome."</div>
    <div class="troubleshooting-a">Re-bake the terrain using the updated <code>DPT_SurfaceDataBaker</code>[cite: 9]. Earlier versions only stored a single precomputed dominant byte per triangle, which lacked the multi-biome candidate arrays required for real-time runtime re-evaluation[cite: 9].</div>

    <div class="troubleshooting-q">"Setting a Weight Multiplier to 0.0 makes other biomes disappear or cut off sharply."</div>
    <div class="troubleshooting-a">In a multiplicative weighting pipeline, <code>1.0</code> represents neutral baseline coverage[cite: 6]. Setting a multiplier to <code>0.0</code> erases that biome completely from the face[cite: 6]. If that biome was blending with a secondary biome, the secondary biome will take 100% of the normalized weight[cite: 6]. To disable a dynamic slot without modifying underlying painted weights, uncheck the slot's active toggle or set its Target ID to <code>-1</code>[cite: 6].</div>

    <div class="troubleshooting-q">"The on-screen control hint box overlaps the Raycast Tester HUD."</div>
    <div class="troubleshooting-a">The <code>DPT_Terrain_DemoCamera</code> overlay is anchored to the bottom-center of the viewport, while <code>DPT_SurfaceRaycastTester</code> renders in the top-left corner. Ensure both scripts are updated to the latest version to prevent viewport rect overlap.</div>

